      "problem": "Find $p$ if $5$ is a root of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}+4px-10.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=5$ is a root, we have $f(5)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=5,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(5)^{2}+4p(5)-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(25)+20p-10 & =0 \\\\ 150+20p-10 & =0 \\\\ 140+20p & =0 \\\\ 20p & =-140 \\\\ p & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
